<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brigantia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brigantia was a Celtic goddess worshipped in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in the Roman period, known from inscriptions and a relief found at Birrens in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>. Her name, meaning 'the high one', is linked to that of the Brigantes, whose patron deity she probably was, and Roman worshippers identified her with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minerva">Minerva</a> and Victory. She is often connected with the Irish goddess Brigid.</p></div>
